  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(¬X∧Y)∨(¬X∧Z)?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can factor out the conjunction with $¬X,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(¬X∧Y)∨(¬X∧Z)≡¬X∧(Y∨Z)\n$$",
